- Required closure: persistent per-digest adopter claim/journal and restart reconciliation; valid-existing/invalid-existing/missing branches; same-FD write/readback hash; post-open parent/ancestor identity checks through rename; no-replace publication and parent durability seal; bounded `scandir` enumeration and durable partial-mutation/residue evidence on unexpected exceptions. [Task 2]

## Failures and how to do differently

- `O_EXCL` plus `RENAME_EXCL` does not establish unique adopter or crash recovery. R2 found fixed temp `EEXIST` after pre-rename crash, nonsealed post-rename/pre-parent-fsync restart, no durable claim/reconciler, no write-side same-FD readback, and mutation-parent TOCTOU. Therefore `[ROLLUP:CACHE-PREP-V1:S3:R2-TECH] FAIL / BLOCKED`. [Task 2]
